 goals go on dates and generally  do things that are more interesting than  binge watching seasons of their latest  Netflix obsession but the second reality  show within the show relieves that  tension Terry's house provides us with a  panel of commentators who are proxies  for the viewers they are viewers of the  show and we get to watch them watch and  talk about what they watched this  appears to the viewer as a real reality  it's your reality or at least a better  mirror of your very reality while you're  watching the show than what goes on in  the house is the reality of this panel  is so obvious and so like our own that  even though the panel is the more unique  and unusual element of the show its  presence is never explained while the  premise of the house is restated in  every episode the ideal the panel  presents is one you can live up to while  you're watching your demo ami-chan got  to saw you never gonna tell uncle Murray  will you tell a meetin as high as you  take you know  the panel teaches you how to watch the  show guides your perspective of the show  and provides you with a simulation of  watching a show with friends but perhaps  most critically if we buy into Wallace's  theory it seems to validate your  existence and actions as a passive  consumer in order to be like the people  on TV you don't have to turn off Netflix  go make attractive friends do fun things  with them go on dates you can just watch  other people do those things and all you  have to do is judge and make comments  about their actions laugh at their  mishaps and express frustrations when  they do frustrating things and this all  must be valid because that's what those  people on TV are doing commentators have  long existed as part of TV but they've  almost always tried to present  themselves as being in a privileged  position they are on TV commentating  because they are experts or celebrities  some of the terrace house panel are  celebrities but they don't appeal to  that advantage to make their commentary  they are presented as the viewers equal  they sit not behind a fancy desk on a  massive set overlooking a fake skyline  but in a mock living room sitting on  couches and pillows as you might if you  had some friends over to watch the show  with you  much of online commentary content is the  same type of reality TV giving the  audience an on screen viewer in the same  way that Terrace house does these  commentators reinforce the ideal of the  consumer while allowing us to consume  the same content we wanted to before you  laugh you lose and other people's your  life you lose that's right we're gonna  react to people reacting to things and  see who laughs first and you're gonna  watch me reactiveness pudy pie presents  himself as just a bro in a room with a  computer watching stuff and playing  games not very far removed from what his  audience looks like when they're  consuming his content the passive  consumer is guided trained and comforted  by the commentary it turns out what we  wanted to see on TV all along was  ourselves but that's a problem because  we're boring the solution put someone  like us on TV alongside the content we  originally wanted to see  I want to be clear that this is not a  doom and gloom message about commentary  content what exactly it's doing and why  it's arisen is psychologically complex  and I'm only examining one possible  reason for why it's risen to prominence  recently in this video but there's a lot  more here and I don't think Wallace's  theory of TV's problem and commentary  content as a solution tells the whole  story in part two I want to discuss  commentary culture outside of streaming  video and how I think the medium of the  internet encourages commentary content  and I want to examine the role of the  video essay as part of commentary  content and why it might just be the  thing we need in the midst of our  growing media consumption and in the  spirit of talking about commentary  culture I want to try to integrate what  you have to say into this series so  leave your comment below and I might  include it in the next video maybe you  feel like you've been consuming too much  commentary content if you want to take a  step back and consume something  different and learn a skill while you're  at it I recommend trying Skillshare  whatever it is you want to learn skill  share has you covered with over 22,000  courses on a wide variety of topics  Skillshare is one of the best places on  the internet to learn or improve a skill  recently I've really enjoyed Aaron tre  plans courses on customizing type and  logo design they're entertaining and  I've learned a lot that has helped me  with the little bits of graphic design I  have to do for YouTube and video editing  Premium Membership for Skillshare starts  around $10 a month but for the first 100  people to use the link in my description  you can get two months of Skillshare for  free these usually go quickly so jump in  there while you can  and finally thank you to my patreon  supporters if you want to get one of  these little stickers and listen to the  podcast head over to patreon.com/scishow  Thomas flight
 

